{
  "_comment": [
    "How to rebuild the demo corpus after a wipe. Every field here is an ingest",
    "label the extractor cannot infer from the document text -- matter_id, source,",
    "source_type and date_of_event are captured at the door and override anything",
    "the model emits (ARCHITECTURE section 8). Losing this file means re-deriving",
    "all of it by hand.",
    "",
    "Two transcripts share matter 2025-CH-01188 on purpose: Brightwater is one",
    "matter heard twice, and that is what makes it a case-lifecycle test rather",
    "than two unrelated hearings.",
    "",
    "Run with tools/ingest_batch.py. Ingest costs roughly $0.06 a transcript, so a",
    "full rebuild of this manifest is about $1.00. Prefer",
    "tools/snapshot_memories.py --restore when the change being tested is",
    "downstream of extraction."
  ],
